WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.690
Aizawa.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.310
Here.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.310
Akaishi.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:05.980
Here.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.110
Amami.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.770
Amami?

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.030
Hey, Amami.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.650
Here.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.320
Is something wrong, Amami?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.450
You've had trouble focusing lately.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.370
I'm sorry.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.680
I'm so hungry!

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.850
Let's have lunch together, Amami.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.020
Sorry, Ogawa.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.980
I need to take care of something.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.490
Amami...

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.040
Do you think Amami forgot her lunch?!

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.000
She's been doing this every day lately.
Don't do it, Amami!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.870
If you try to fill up on tap water,
you'll just make yourself sick!
She's been doing this every day lately.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.170
She just wanders around the school,
like she's searching for something.
If you try to fill up on tap water,
you'll just make yourself sick!

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.540
And you guys! Pick on me already!
She just wanders around the school,
like she's searching for something.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:32.170
And you guys! Pick on me already!

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.340
I'm trying to lighten the mood here!

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.170
At first, I was wondering what the joke was.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.010
Are you listening?
At first, I was wondering what the joke was.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:38.300
Hey!
At first, I was wondering what the joke was.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.090
Yeah...
Hey!

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:39.260
Hey!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.680
Come on, you guys!

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.610
I guess Amami really <i>did</i> lose her sixth sense.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.740
This must be another effect of that.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.280
I can't capture ghosts on camera anymore,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.160
and there are no signs of spiritual activity.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:08.120
Even though the roll-call samurai and
the gal ghost are probably right up there...

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.340
It's a good thing!

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.210
Life's been too crazy with them around.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.090
Yeah, so you say,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.220
but I bet you're sad you can't
see your grandma anymore.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.260
Nana's still here!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.140
She's watching over me,
even if I can't see her!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.310
What is it?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.730
Nothing.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.690
Just thinking that Inoue's really changed.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:36.820
No kidding.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.950
Before, she just insisted that
there was no such thing as ghosts.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.950
That probably goes for all of us.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.540
The school and the town seem so quiet now,

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.960
even though that's really the norm.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.840
We'd never have realized the truth
if Amami hadn't shown us...

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.220
That even though we can't see them,

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.600
there are so many interesting
personalities all around us.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.510
I think I'm pretty interesting!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.440
It's all thanks to Amami.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.190
They ignored me again...

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.030
It's thanks to Amami...

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.030
Maybe you're right.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.700
That's why...

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.700
That forced smile on her face

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.120
somehow really bothers me.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.250
Amami!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.460
We heard Amami passed out!

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.720
Shh!

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.510
Quiet in the infirmary!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.550
I couldn't find anything wrong.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:50.350
I assume her anxiety got the best of her.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.310
Anxiety?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.360
Her guardian is coming to get her,

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.690
so you should all get back to class.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.400
Let's go.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.910
She must be anxious about you-know-what.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.870
What else could it be?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.120
You guys are awfully mean to me...

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.960
No peeking at a sleeping girl!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.630
E-Everyone...

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:19.920
Amami?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.550
Hey, are you okay?

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.180
Where... are you...

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.550
Come out... Say something...

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.810
Please...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.520
We're all right here!

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.400
Not us, huh...

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.530
She can't even see them in her dreams.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:43.900
Amami...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.490
Amami's out sick today?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.540
After what happened yesterday, I'm not surprised.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:55.410
Hey, why don't we all go visit her after school?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.960
I'm in.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.670
You'll come with us, right, Inoue?

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.300
Y-Yeah...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.800
I'm sorry. I know you came all this way...

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.010
Um, may I ask why we can't see Amami?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.100
Is she that sick?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:17.650
No, the doctor said it's just a mild case of anxiety.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.860
She's resting in her room right now.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.070
Then why can't we...

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.570
Hibiki said...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:33.450
"I can't face everyone after making
them worry about me so much."

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.830
And "I'm sorry."

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.580
What the heck?

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:42.380
Why? Why is she apologizing?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.470
She's always worrying about others, even when they don't ask...

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.590
And now she says...

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.140
Don't be stupid!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:58.190
Inoue, I'm sure Hibiki realizes that.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:04.230
But now that she can't see the ghosts
who have been near her all her life...

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.360
I don't think she knows how to handle it yet.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.660
I myself have no idea what to say to her.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.500
She hasn't been eating well these past few days, either.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.830
She hasn't been eating?

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.840
Not since the Star Festival.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.460
If nothing changes, she'll just grow weaker...

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.840
Um...

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.630
We'll be going now.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.350
Please take care of Amami.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.570
It's really frustrating that
we can't do anything for her.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.900
If only Amami could get her
sixth sense back somehow...

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:54.280
How are some run-of-the-mill high school kids
supposed to restore someone's sixth sense?

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.910
I'm concerned that she's not eating, too.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.500
Yeah. That's the more pressing issue.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.670
Oh, yeah!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.040
Hey, Inoue!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.500
That cousin you told us about before...

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.670
You mean Yuuki?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:12.470
You and Amami cooked for him because
he was a really fussy eater, right?

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.930
What about it?

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:19.430
I just thought if we did the same thing,
Amami might eat for us...

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.730
No way!

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:25.520
I didn't even know why Yuuki was so
hung up on that dish until Amami tol—

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:29.280
But yeah, they're really good.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.240
I'm so glad you like them.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.620
They're actually...

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.450
They're very special to me...

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.710
What's wrong, Inoue?

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.790
Sorry, there's something I need to do.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.920
You guys can go on ahead!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:51.380
Yes?

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.220
Who's...

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.510
Oh... Inoue?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.470
Why are you so out of breath?

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.980
Did you forget something?

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:04.980
I...

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:12.070
I have a favor to ask.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.330
Guess we all had the same idea.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.460
Well, there's nothing we can do for Amami.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:31.170
So all we can do now is help
with the stuff she can't do herself.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.800
I've got the Noritama offering!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:33.670
Here!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.010
Just like that.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.010
Let's clean up, then.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.430
We've got a lot more places to get to.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.350
Where's Inoue?

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.930
Oh, of course!

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.440
It was your friends,

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.990
the roll-call samurai, the gal ghost,

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.870
and so many more that
gave me the push to do this.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.450
My friends did?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.580
I'm relieved.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:12.330
You were able to connect to
so many people in my absence.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.500
Yes.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.340
They're all very dear to me.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.010
But now they're gone,

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.930
all because of my selfish wish.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.640
We're no longer connected.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:38.240
Amami, get your butt out here already!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.990
Inoue?!

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.330
Get that weak look off your face.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:56.340
Eat some food, and get your strength back.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.010
They...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.260
They all looked so happy
whenever they ate their offerings.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.510
And that, in turn, made <i>me</i> happy...

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:09.600
But...

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.730
Now...

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.030
I can only see them in my memories.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.900
And I'm still...

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.500
Get off your high horse

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.830
and eat something!

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.500
Eat it right now!

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.760
Now chew it up!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:00.190
Something told me this was probably
what you wanted to eat most right now.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:17.960
The fried eggs you made for Yuuki that one time
were your mom's recipe, weren't they?

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.960
I...

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.970
When I thought of how they can't eat...

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.470
I felt it wasn't fair that only I could...

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.470
But...

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:38.980
It's good.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.360
It's delicious.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.730
Of course it is!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.240
Because you're alive!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.450
And they all feel the same way!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.410
Inoue...

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.630
These feelings don't just run one way.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.550
I've always known that.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.260
Everyone, alive or dead,

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.050
shares a bond through the same feelings.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:15.100
And through my sixth sense,
I can confirm those bonds are real.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:21.690
But I can't see them
or hear their voices anymore.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.700
I've never once thought about
what I'd be without my sixth sense.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.070
And now that I've lost those precious bonds,

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.450
I don't even know who
I'm supposed to be from now on...

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.460
I'm so lost...

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.830
So scared...

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.670
That's why you holed up in your room
and wouldn't even see us?

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.090
I didn't want to worry you any further.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:53.470
We wouldn't have become friends
if it weren't for my sixth sense.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.850
So now that I've lost it, now that I have nothing,

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.770
I wasn't sure if our friendships would survive...

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.200
Let's go, Amami.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.660
Go where?

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.370
There are people I want you to see.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.450
Please, wait... I...

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.290
Sorry, Amami.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.330
I'm <i>this</i> close to snapping right now.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.960
R-Right!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.670
Um, where are we going?

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.220
You'll see.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.680
Oh, Inoue and Amami.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.640
Huh? Mr. Moriya?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.140
Hello.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:42.310
What a relief.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:46.020
I heard you were out sick yesterday,
but you seem fine now.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.280
Still, don't overdo it.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.610
Are you guys out on a date?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:51.860
Oh...

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:53.700
Well...

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.490
We're going to make an announcement.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.120
Congratulations!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.420
You mean...

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:07.000
I never had the courage to go back
to the place where I'd stayed with her.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:12.050
But since she came to see me...

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.970
I felt it was my turn this time.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.980
I see.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.390
And we have you to thank, Amami.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:27.020
That's right. You reconnected us.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.360
I'm sure she'll be thrilled.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:33.990
Yeah...

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.370
Hibiki?

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.120
I thought it was you.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:45.080
I was worried since I hadn't
seen you at the supermarket lately.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.710
I'm sorry for worrying you.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.670
Out shopping with your friend?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.170
I'm making meat and potatoes tonight.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:56.140
Every now and then,
I feel like my daughter comes home.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.390
The gal ghost?

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:02.180
So I can't be lazy with my cooking!

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.890
It really isn't easy.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.150
Thank you, Hibiki.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.200
Sir...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.280
You again?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.410
What's that?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:23.290
I've got no relation to this kid whatsoever, but...

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.630
Just a whim.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.250
Anyway, young lady!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.420
Y-Yes?!

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.460
Your spirits are too low!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:35.260
You're still young, so straighten up!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.180
Have some nasty chocolate or something.

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:41.970
Um, Inoue, were these the people you wanted me to see?

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:43.270
Nope.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.060
They were all total coincidences.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.560
But now maybe you see how you—

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.820
Narumi! Hibiki!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:53.780
And there they are.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:55.780
Is that...

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.160
How have you been?

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.160
Yuuki! It's nice to see you again.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.410
Is this your sister?

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.920
Yeah! Look how big she is!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.000
Sorry for the short notice.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.300
It's cool.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.420
I wanted to show Kyouka off to Hibiki, anyway.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.220
Your name is Kyouka?

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.890
This is the first time we've really gotten to talk.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.430
My name is Amami Hibiki...

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.560
"Kyouka"?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.690
The characters mean "an echoing song."

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.900
The first character in her name is the same as yours.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.190
My name...

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:38.450
I never really thanked you properly, so... Thanks!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.450
Because of you, I've been a really good big brother!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.040
Yuuki...

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.710
Hi-mi-ki!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.080
Did she just talk?!

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.590
That's awesome, Kyouka!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.880
See you later!

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.850
And I'm sorry I said your eggs were gross!

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:05.390
They were actually really yummy!

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:10.650
Do you see how you're still connected?

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:15.030
Yuuki and everyone else,
they all care very deeply for you.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.150
So are you still going to cry
about your sixth sense?

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.950
But I don't have anything else...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.780
Don't be stupid!

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.700
<i>You</i> were the one who brought them together!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.170
Maybe it was the sixth sense at first,

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:37.260
but it was you, and you alone, who actually
formed their connections to the ghosts!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.050
You, Amami Hibiki.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:44.640
Nosy, soft-hearted,
oblivious, and infinitely kind.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:50.640
And it's because you're you that,
even though you still completely terrify me,

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.150
I want to be friends with you forever!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.150
Inoue...

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:03.450
You really don't mind... staying connected to me?

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.200
Of course not.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:09.500
You're allowed to be a little selfish, you know.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.460
If I really can...

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.710
Then I want to stay friends with you all,

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:21.260
and the ghosts, even if I can't see them!

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.480
Lady Amami.

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.980
'Sup, Hibby?

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.980
Amami!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.440
What's the matter? You look terrible.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.490
Everyone...

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:53.500
All right, let's check out those panties!

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.670
For crying out loud...

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.840
Well, I can't blame you for being happy.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.470
We, too, wish to stay forever by your side.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.340
Everyone...

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.350
I guess I was already connected to them, huh?

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.100
Oh, Amami!

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:19.320
I'm so glad you're doing better!

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:22.570
Good to see that things are already lively again.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.820
Well, this is how it should be.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.450
Yes, I believe so.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:36.540
With or without her sixth sense,
Hibiki will be fine now.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.000
<i>They've all been here with me.</i>

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:45.090
<i>They stayed connected to me.</i>

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:02.610
<i>Don't cry if you can't see them.</i>

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:08.740
<i>Don't be sad if you can't see them.</i>

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:14.370
<i>Kind feelings, warm feelings,</i>

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.660
<i>feelings of love...</i>

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>They are feelings everyone has
that bind them to someone.</i>

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:28.760
<i>We can't see them, but they're right there.</i>

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:34.470
<i>Should you still worry that they might not be,</i>

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:37.100
<i>just hold out your hand,</i>

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.270
<i>and they'll surely...</i>

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.910
Is something wrong?

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:55.410
Would you like to tell me about it?

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:45.810
A lot has happened, but I'm so glad
I get to spend time with everyone again.

00:23:45.810 --> 00:23:48.320
Amami, hurry up!

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:50.440
Everyone else is ready!

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:51.990
Let's get going!

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:54.860
The amusement park isn't
gonna run away, you know.

00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:57.080
I think <i>you're</i> more likely to run away, Inoue.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:58.990
Because of that one attraction...

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:01.160
Sh-Shut up!

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:05.210
The final episode of Re-Kan!:
"Summer Memories."

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.300
I hope today will bring us
another wonderful connection.
